      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A historic watering trough in Manns Choice once fed horses pulling stagecoaches across Glades Pike to Pittsburgh, a relic of the town’s stagecoach era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manns_Choice%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Historic Manns Choice Schoolhouse, built in the late 1800s, stands as a testament to the community’s early commitment to education.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
